Structure matrix2: Field a as long integer. Field b as long integer. Field c as long integer. Field d as long integer. End structure.
Structure bignum: Field digits as array of long integer with length 40. Field length as long integer. End structure.
Enumeration grade: Enumerator platinum. Enumerator gold as 20. Enumerator silver. Enumerator bronze as 50. End enumeration.

Procedure mmul takes left as structure matrix2 right as structure matrix2 returns structure matrix2:
  Declare product as structure matrix2.
  Set member a of product to Member a of left times Member a of right plus Member b of left times Member c of right.
  Set member b of product to Member a of left times Member b of right plus Member b of left times Member d of right.
  Set member c of product to Member c of left times Member a of right plus Member d of left times Member c of right.
  Set member d of product to Member c of left times Member b of right plus Member d of left times Member d of right.
  Return product.
End procedure.
Procedure mpow takes base as structure matrix2 power as integer returns structure matrix2:
  If power is equal to 1 then: Return base. End if.
  Declare half as structure matrix2 with value Call mpow with base (power divided by 2) done.
  Declare squared as structure matrix2 with value Call mmul with half half done.
  If power minus (power divided by 2 times 2) is not equal to 0 then: Return Call mmul with squared base done. End if.
  Return squared.
End procedure.

Procedure compatible takes board as array of long integer with length 8 candidate as long integer check as long integer returns long integer:
  Declare i as long integer with value 0.
  While i is less than check:
    If Element at i in board is equal to candidate then: Return 0. End if.
    If check minus i is equal to absolute value of (candidate minus Element at i in board) then: Return 0. End if.
    Add 1 to i.
  End while.
  Return 1.
End procedure.
Procedure queens takes n as long integer board as array of long integer with length 8 returns long integer:
  If n is equal to 8 then: Return 1. End if.
  Declare solutions as long integer with value 0.
  Declare candidate as long integer with value 0.
  While candidate is less than 8:
    If Call compatible with board candidate n done is not equal to 0 then:
      Set element at n in board to candidate.
      Add Call queens with n plus 1 board done to solutions.
    End if.
    Add 1 to candidate.
  End while.
  Return solutions.
End procedure.

Procedure partition takes lo as integer hi as integer a as array of integer with length 12 returns integer:
  Declare pivot as integer with value Element at hi in a.
  Declare i as integer with value lo.
  Declare j as integer with value lo.
  Declare t as integer with value 0.
  While j is less than hi:
    If Element at j in a is less than pivot then:
      Set t to Element at i in a.
      Set element at i in a to Element at j in a.
      Set element at j in a to t.
      Add 1 to i.
    End if.
    Add 1 to j.
  End while.
  Set t to Element at i in a.
  Set element at i in a to Element at hi in a.
  Set element at hi in a to t.
  Return i.
End procedure.
Procedure quicksort takes lo as integer hi as integer a as array of integer with length 12 returns void:
  If lo is less than hi then:
    Declare k as integer with value Call partition with lo hi a done.
    Call quicksort with lo (k minus 1) a done.
    Call quicksort with (k plus 1) hi a done.
  End if.
  Return.
End procedure.
Procedure search takes lo as integer hi as integer key as integer a as array of integer with length 12 returns integer:
  If lo is greater than hi then: Return 0. End if.
  Declare mid as integer with value lo plus (hi minus lo divided by 2).
  If Element at mid in a is equal to key then: Return 1. End if.
  If Element at mid in a is less than key then: Return Call search with mid plus 1 hi key a done. End if.
  Return Call search with lo (mid minus 1) key a done.
End procedure.

Procedure bigfactorial returns structure bignum:
  Declare result as structure bignum with members length as 1 done.
  Set element at 0 in Member digits of result to 1.
  Declare factor as long integer with value 2.
  Declare carry as long integer with value 0.
  Declare i as long integer with value 0.
  Declare len as long integer with value 1.
  Declare here as long integer with value 0.
  Declare next as long integer with value 0.
  While factor is less than or equal to 25:
    Set carry to 0.
    Set i to 0.
    Set len to Member length of result.
    While i is less than len:
      Set here to Element at i in Member digits of result.
      Set next to here times factor plus carry.
      Set element at i in Member digits of result to next mod 1000000000.
      Set carry to next divided by 1000000000.
      Add 1 to i.
    End while.
    While carry is greater than 0:
      Set len to Member length of result.
      Set element at len in Member digits of result to carry mod 1000000000.
      Set carry to carry divided by 1000000000.
      Set member length of result to len plus 1.
    End while.
    Add 1 to factor.
  End while.
  Return result.
End procedure.

Say "Phase 1: Primes at work".
Say "====================".
Declare sieve as array of boolean with length 200.
Set c to 0.
While c is less than 200:
  Set element at c in sieve to true.
  Add 1 to c.
End while.
Set element at 0 in sieve to false.
Set element at 1 in sieve to false.
Set p to 2.
While p times p is less than 200:
  If Element at p in sieve then:
    Set m to p times p.
    While m is less than 200:
      Set element at m in sieve to false.
      Add p to m.
    End while.
  End if.
  Add 1 to p.
End while.
Set count to 0.
Set sum to 0.
Set largest to 0.
For n from 2 to 199:
  If Element at n in sieve then:
    Add 1 to count.
    Add n to sum.
    Set largest to n.
  End if.
End for.
Say "There are" followed by count followed by "primes below 200.".
Say "Their sum is" followed by sum followed by "and the largest is" followed by largest.

Say "Phase 2: Sorting and searching".
Say "==============================".
Declare numbers as array of integer with length 12 with values 37 followed by 8 followed by 101 followed by 3 followed by 42 followed by 17 followed by 96 followed by 13 followed by 55 followed by 7 followed by 90 followed by 29 done.
Call quicksort with 0 11 numbers done.
Say "Sorted numbers:".
For i from 0 to 11:
  Say Element at i in numbers.
End for.
Say "Search results follow.".
Say "42:" followed by Call search with 0 11 42 numbers done.
Say "7:" followed by Call search with 0 11 7 numbers done.
Say "99:" followed by Call search with 0 11 99 numbers done.
Say "90:" followed by Call search with 0 11 90 numbers done.

Say "Phase 3: Eight queens".
Say "======================".
Declare board as array of long integer with length 8.
Say "The eight queens puzzle has" followed by Call queens with 0 board done followed by "distinct solutions.".

Say "Phase 4: Fibonacci through matrix powers".
Say "=========================================".
Declare identity as structure matrix2 with members a as 1 followed by b as 1 followed by c as 1 followed by d as 0 done.
Declare powered as structure matrix2 with value Call mpow with identity 30 done.
Say "Fibonacci(30) is" followed by Member c of powered.

Say "Phase 5: A modest big integer".
Say "==============================".
Declare fact as structure bignum with value Call bigfactorial done.
Declare totaldigits as long integer with value 0.
Declare top as long integer with value 0.
Declare sumdigits as long integer with value 0.
Declare w as long integer with value 0.
Declare piece as long integer with value 0.
Declare low as long integer with value 0.
Declare tz as long integer with value 0.
Set totaldigits to (Member length of fact minus 1) times 9.
Set top to Element at (Member length of fact minus 1) in Member digits of fact.
While top is greater than 0:
  Add 1 to totaldigits.
  Set top to top divided by 10.
End while.
Say "25! has" followed by totaldigits followed by "decimal digits.".
While w is less than Member length of fact:
  Set piece to Element at w in Member digits of fact.
  While piece is greater than 0:
    Add piece mod 10 to sumdigits.
    Set piece to piece divided by 10.
  End while.
  Add 1 to w.
End while.
Say "The sum of its decimal digits is" followed by sumdigits.
Set w to 0.
Set low to Element at 0 in Member digits of fact.
While low is equal to 0:
  Add 9 to tz.
  Add 1 to w.
  Set low to Element at w in Member digits of fact.
End while.
While low mod 10 is equal to 0:
  Add 1 to tz.
  Set low to low divided by 10.
End while.
Say "It ends in" followed by tz followed by "zeroes.".
Say "The low base-one-billion group is" followed by Element at 0 in Member digits of fact followed by "and the next is" followed by Element at 1 in Member digits of fact.

Say "Phase 6: Lists and grades".
Say "==========================".
Set squares to Empty list of numbers.
For n from 1 to 5:
  Append n times n to squares.
End for.
Say "Squares one to five:" followed by Item at 1 in squares followed by Item at 2 in squares followed by Item at 3 in squares followed by Item at 4 in squares followed by Item at 5 in squares.
Replace item at 3 in squares with 100.
Say "After change, the list holds" followed by Length of squares followed by "values and the third value is" followed by Item at 3 in squares.
Set rank to Enumerator bronze of grade.
Switch rank:
  When 20: Say "twenty or gold". Break.
  When 50: Say "fifty or bronze". Break.
  Otherwise: Say "some other rank". Break.
End switch.
Switch 100:
  When 50: Say "fifty or bronze". Break.
  Otherwise: Say "one hundred defaults". Break.
End switch.